# 24. Initial Research Gaps

The baseline identifies several areas requiring deeper research.

### Gap 1 — National watershed condition

There is no single universally accepted national measure of overall watershed ecological condition.

### Gap 2 — Groundwater–surface-water integration

Monitoring and governance frequently remain divided.

### Gap 3 — Ecological-flow performance

Environmental-flow objectives are not consistently represented in national performance measures.

### Gap 4 — Biological outcomes

Water-quality programs often have stronger administrative and chemical indicators than long-term biological outcome measures.

### Gap 5 — Attribution

Watershed responses are influenced by many simultaneous variables.

### Gap 6 — Cost-effectiveness

The comparative effectiveness of watershed interventions is not consistently evaluated.

### Gap 7 — Long-term persistence

Projects are often easier to document than decades-long ecological maintenance.

### Gap 8 — Cross-jurisdiction performance

It remains difficult to determine whether multi-government watershed institutions consistently outperform fragmented approaches.

